    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/air_temperature_na/legend.png?v=na-tmp-20261012-0045-gdps-GDPS_15km_AirTemp_2m-n-381512-hrrr-hrrr-hrrr.20261011-23-n-698318-rrfs_rrfs-ak-rrfs.20261011-18-n-678937-rrfs_rrfs-conus-rrfs.20261011-18-n-0-rrfs_rrfs-na-rrfs.20261011-18-n-452374" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Air temperature 2m (MODEL analysis, NOT direct observation): <b>LOWEST -60F</b> blue-white &rarr; freezing wall 30-40F &rarr; yellows 70-85F &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 150F</b> pink/red. Same F, same color, every source.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis, HRRR + RRFS-NA, GDPS fallback)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3km 2m analysis (CONUS domain) + NOAA RRFS North American output (broad domain) + ECCC GDPS 15km fallback<br/><a href="https://gsl.noaa.gov/rrfs/">https://gsl.noaa.gov/rrfs/</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
